Negative control for `SELF` never being refused by the matrix gate (`R7-14`,
the over-refusal side).

Reads the matrix cell for `SELF` like any other actor. Every module in the tree
leaves `SELF` `null as never` — it names no actor at all, the scope builder
resolves it to whoever is active — so the gate then refuses the BARE route every
page boots on, and a logged-out landing draws "not available at this scope"
where the auth gate belongs (`R7-1`). Nothing throws and `/as/client` still
resolves, so only the SELF clause is on trial.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the bare-route cases — the playground shell no longer draws a table inside
the forced canvas, and the port booted with no `/as/` segment publishes
`isServed: false` instead of the cell's own state. The `/as/guest` refusal case
still passes, so the control cannot go red by serving everything.

